  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This star is made from six pieces: one flat cylinder centre and five cone points. All pieces are worked in "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "continuous-rounds-star"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "continuous rounds"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " starting from a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring-star"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Once stuffed and sewn at even intervals, the result is a firm five-pointed star that holds its shape without a frame."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Gold or metallic DK yarn, approx. 35 g"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "3.5 mm crochet hook"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Polyester toy stuffing"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Stitch marker, tapestry needle, scissors"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Centre disc (cylinder)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring-star"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " with 6 dc. Increase to 30 dc over five rounds. Work two straight rounds, keeping the piece flat. Decrease with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "dc2tog-star"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "dc2tog"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " back to 6 dc. Stuff lightly so the disc remains fairly flat. Close and leave a long tail."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Points (make 5)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "For each point, make a magic ring with 6 dc. Increase to 18 dc over two rounds. Work two even rounds. Decrease back to 6 dc, stuffing before the gap closes. Fasten off with a long tail."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Assembly"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Mark five evenly spaced positions around the edge of the centre disc. Sew each cone base to one marked position using "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "whip-stitch-star"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "whip stitch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Pull the tail through to the disc centre and knot off. Adjust the angles so each point radiates evenly outward."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Thread a length of yarn through the tip of one point and knot into a hanging loop. The star can also stand upright if placed with two points at the base."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The Christmas tree amigurumi uses a similar cone-point technique. A set of stars in different sizes makes an easy garland project."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
